274
00:14:35.116 --> 00:14:37.563
Well. I like how everything's sepia-toned.

275
00:14:37.566 --> 00:14:39.413
Makes  me feel all nostalgic.

276
00:14:39.465 --> 00:14:43.440
I never thought it would come to this
when I fought in the first World War.

277
00:14:43.546 --> 00:14:45.750
First World War?
Why you keep callin' it that?

278
00:14:45.855 --> 00:14:47.832
Oh. you'll see.

279
00:14:53.048 --> 00:14:55.841
We interrupt this dance music
from the Meridian Room

280
00:14:55.847 --> 00:14:58.063
in Capital City's
fabulous Hotel Hitler

281
00:14:58.065 --> 00:14:59.642
to bring you a special bulletin.

282
00:14:59.646 --> 00:15:01.413
Hey. I'm not done dancing.

283
00:15:01.417 --> 00:15:03.710
This bulletin better swing.

284
00:15:03.815 --> 00:15:06.431
Reports are coming in
of giant metal cylin landing

285
00:15:06.435 --> 00:15:08.263
on the outskirts
of major American cities.

286
00:15:09.318 --> 00:15:10.313
Cylinders?

287
00:15:10.617 --> 00:15:12.510
Astronomers say
the ominous capsules

288
00:15:12.515 --> 00:15:14.631
originated from Earth's
closest neighbor.

289
00:15:15.075 --> 00:15:17.411
- Flanders?
- Mars.

290
00:15:18.865 --> 00:15:20.263
So.  it's a war of the worlds.

291
00:15:22.015 --> 00:15:23.763
Good thing we got the sun on our side.

292
00:15:26.568 --> 00:15:28.612
Go ahead and hide. you coward.

293
00:15:29.915 --> 00:15:31.813
I'm in the small town
of Grover's Mill.

294
00:15:31.817 --> 00:15:34.213
where a crowd has gathered
around one of the strange

295
00:15:34.217 --> 00:15:35.313
Martian cylinders.

296
00:15:35.615 --> 00:15:37.762
It's opening.
A tentacle is emerging.

297
00:15:39.865 --> 00:15:40.912
Settle down. children.

298
00:15:40.915 --> 00:15:43.232
Have a cigarette to calm your nerves.

299
00:15:45.218 --> 00:15:46.213
Oh. my stars.

300
00:15:46.215 --> 00:15:48.310
It's firing a beam
of pure energy.

301
00:15:48.916 --> 00:15:50.613
It's burning people alive.

302
00:15:53.617 --> 00:15:54.661
Okay. boys. we're under attack.

303
00:15:54.666 --> 00:15:57.240
Let's drive 'em out of town
the way we did with the Irish.

304
00:15:57.287 --> 00:15:58.840
Hey. I'm Irish.

305
00:16:00.518 --> 00:16:01.513
Oh. wait. I'm Polish.

306
00:16:04.117 --> 00:16:05.673
The devastation is incredible.

307
00:16:05.677 --> 00:16:08.310
They're grinding up the
bodies of human beings.

308
00:16:09.617 --> 00:16:11.582
Now they're riding horses in the rain.

309
00:16:12.917 --> 00:16:16.261
Now they're playing the xylophone
while bowling near an airport

310
00:16:21.295 --> 00:16:22.812
Now. before we all die.

311
00:16:22.915 --> 00:16:26.262
one last selection from the Nathan Newley Orchestra.

312
00:16:26.508 --> 00:16:31.432
I'm  young and healthy
And you've got charms...

313
00:16:32.596 --> 00:16:35.493
Gee. Mr. Welles.
this sure is a swell show

314
00:16:35.496 --> 00:16:36.573
you're puttin' on for the folks.

315
00:16:36.805 --> 00:16:39.712
Well. I just hope our saucy lile radio prank

316
00:16:39.717 --> 00:16:42.862
will give these "folks." as
you call them. a giggle. a gasp.

317
00:16:42.866 --> 00:16:45.910
and provide a good lead-in
for Misters Amos and Andy.

318
00:16:50.068 --> 00:16:51.362
Burn everything.

319
00:16:51.568 --> 00:16:54.513
You know. Homer.
we haven't actually seen these aliens.

320
00:16:54.518 --> 00:16:56.331
That's alien talk.

321
00:16:57.206 --> 00:17:00.011
"Big Band Stu." says 23 Skidoo.

322
00:17:01.566 --> 00:17:03.060
We have nothing to fear

323
00:17:03.465 --> 00:17:07.160
but the aliens and their vastly
superior killing technology.

324
00:17:07.367 --> 00:17:09.613
Boys. we have to assume our guns are useless.

325
00:17:09.615 --> 00:17:10.560
Throw 'em in the lake.

326
00:17:12.516 --> 00:17:13.761
Good. Now. the police car.

327
00:17:18.475 --> 00:17:20.530
Wait. did you get my sweater
out of the front seat?

328
00:17:20.537 --> 00:17:21.531
Uh. yeah.

329
00:17:21.536 --> 00:17:24.311
- Well. where is it?
- I'll go get it.

330
00:17:29.147 --> 00:17:30.772
Wait. I have an idea.

331
00:17:30.966 --> 00:17:35.883
The Martians are only killing humans.
so we should pretend to be animals.

332
00:17:36.165 --> 00:17:37.182
Ingenious.

333
00:17:37.688 --> 00:17:41.712
Everyone. remove your
clothes and wallow in filth.

334
00:18:02.065 --> 00:18:03.690
What is everyone doing?

335
00:18:03.695 --> 00:18:05.510
We're out smarting the Martians.

336
00:18:07.066 --> 00:18:07.861
Martians?

337
00:18:07.865 --> 00:18:10.463
You do know that radio
broadcast was a hoax?

338
00:18:11.276 --> 00:18:15.062
Yeah. it was an Orson Welles radio play
of War of the Worlds.

339
00:18:15.468 --> 00:18:16.462
See.

340
00:18:20.316 --> 00:18:22.911
I'm proud of what I achieved
during my rioting.

341
00:18:25.367 --> 00:18:27.791
It was either kill himor kill no one.

342
00:18:29.865 --> 00:18:31.543
Foolish Earthlings.

343
00:18:31.547 --> 00:18:34.031
Now is the perfect time to strike.

344
00:18:34.138 --> 00:18:35.903
They'll thin kit's another hoax.

345
00:18:47.265 --> 00:18:50.212
Dad. a flying saucer
blew up that statue.

346
00:18:50.315 --> 00:18:52.612
Lisa. that was just a radio show.

347
00:18:52.815 --> 00:18:53.810
Uh. Paw.

348
00:18:58.357 --> 00:19:00.861
Please. you must believe me.
this is no hoax.

349
00:19:00.865 --> 00:19:02.312
This is a real invasion.

350
00:19:02.316 --> 00:19:05.111
Oh. yeah? Why don't I just
punch you in the nose. Bud?

351
00:19:06.415 --> 00:19:07.413
"Nosebud."

352
00:19:08.518 --> 00:19:10.730
Chief. you've got
to alert the military.

353
00:19:10.738 --> 00:19:11.933
Fine. fine.
I'll do it right now.

354
00:19:13.886 --> 00:19:17.092
- US Army. What's the threat?
- Uh. we've been invaded...

355
00:19:17.195 --> 00:19:19.280
by a pompous. radio ham.

356
00:19:20.068 --> 00:19:22.401
How's it feel when the
hoax is on the other foot?

357
00:19:22.407 --> 00:19:24.763
I must admit it's unpleasant.

358
00:19:27.358 --> 00:19:29.561
You fool.
You've doomed us all.

359
00:19:29.665 --> 00:19:31.773
Eh. tell it to the Great
Gildersleeve.

360
00:19:37.718 --> 00:19:39.211
Well. they didn'teat the skin.

361
00:19:39.215 --> 00:19:40.861
That's...that's healthy.

362
00:19:51.338 --> 00:19:52.830
Colonel Kang. your report.

363
00:19:52.838 --> 00:19:54.411
Uh. well...

364
00:19:54.415 --> 00:19:56.913
The Earthlings continue
to resent our presence.

365
00:19:58.316 --> 00:20:00.860
You said we'd be greeted as liberators.

366
00:20:01.365 --> 00:20:02.361
Don't worry.

367
00:20:02.365 --> 00:20:05.191
We still have the people's
hearts and minds.

368
00:20:05.598 --> 00:20:06.591
I don't know.

369
00:20:06.998 --> 00:20:10.113
I'm starting to think
"Operation: Enduring Occupation"

370
00:20:10.116 --> 00:20:13.171
- was a bad idea.
- We had to invade.

371
00:20:13.177 --> 00:20:16.710
They were working on weapons of mass disintegration.

372
00:20:16.717 --> 00:20:18.312
Sure they were.

373
00:20:24.275 --> 00:20:33.461
I don't want to set the world on fire

374
00:20:33.867 --> 00:20:40.193
I just want to start a flame in your heart.

375
00:20:40.197 --> 00:20:41.442
Transcript: Raceman
Trad: Rassman. Gornack

376
00:20:41.447 --> 00:20:42.542
Trad: Rassman. Gornack
Synchro: Job22. Daffy

